    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249-a10">

                <pb facs="0404" n="310" xml:id="pg310"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 238.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mullaly to
                        Colonel Lamont</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>223 <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">East Forty-ninth Street, New
                            York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-06-24"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June</hi> 24, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: As the inclosed letter to the
                    President has reference to a matter of special importance, involving the right
                    of protection of Baron de Seillière, who declared his intention to become a
                    citizen of the United States, I would request as a favor its delivery by you to
                    the President. Baron de Seillière is now in France.</p>
                <p>Very truly, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Mullaly.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
